#4471 merged reports because their subject lines matched. The cause does not come from the subject. It comes from the tenant and the channel.

<Callout kind="warn">
The desk marked one known issue. The table shows a second cause, and that cause has no ticket of its own.
</Callout>

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

## parser

The shared parser reads every date month first. For a day-first tenant, the day and the month come out flipped. That is the cause most of these reports share, so it is what #4471 actually is.

Reports the desk read as a one-day move stay in this count. The table footnotes them. They do not get a separate cause.

## hint

booking-v3 prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under the date field. People type what that hint says, and the form reads the date the tenant's way. That is a different bug from the parser. Those reports were merged into #4471 because the subject matched.

